     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g/day) is about 7 times the maximum daily dose. Each single dose is already in the range that causes acute liver failure and can be fatal. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't think of an indication that would justify it.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 1,000 mg PO three times daily, 650 mg PO every 6 hours, or 1,000 mg PO four times daily right now.\n- **Check the dose with pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason for an unusual dose, a pharmacist or toxicologist should review it before it's ordered.\n- **Treat a suspected overdose.** If the concern is an acetaminophen overdose, that needs urgent care, not this order. Treatment usually involves a serum acetaminophen level and N-acetylcysteine. Poison Control is at 1-800-222-1222 in the US.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
